  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scaling up IOM&#x2019;s electronic-Personal Health Record (e-PHR)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project: Scaling up IOM&#x2019;s electronic-Personal Health Record (e-PHR) funded by Takeda, through the piloting of the IOM e-PHR and related activities, aims at ensuring that inselected countries digital health records for migrants are available, promoting availability of medical data at national and at cross-border level, informing adequate health assessments and provision of care including referrals. The activities will be performed in partnership with national/local health authorities and will be linked and/or integrated whenever possible to the existing HIMS. The IOM e-PHR will promote an overarching migrant sensitive health governance approach/system which will ensure that staff working with migrants (health professionals, social workers, law enforcement) is trained on migration health and on the specific digital solution.</narrative>
  </description>
